### 3. Connection in n8n
*Connections:**
## Relationship between "name" in "nodes" and "connections" in n8n 
 node "name" must be the same as "node" in "connections":
 ```json
 {
    "nodes": [
        {
            "parameters": {},
            "id": "54debeb2-56bc-4bbd-8e77-27c2f5d87eeb",
            "name": "Node 1 Name",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
            "typeVersion": 1,
            "position": [
                -992,
                16
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "options": {}
            },
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
            "typeVersion": 3.4,
            "position": [
                -752,
                16
            ],
            "id": "ff4cc763-26b6-4df4-9ee5-42e9c1478f50",
            "name": "Node 2 Name"
        }
    ],
        "connections": {
        "Node 1 Name": {
            "main": [
                [
                    {
                        "node": "Node 2 Name",
                        "type": "main",
                        "index": 0
                    }
                ]
            ]
        }
    },
}
 ```
 As in the example, you can see "name": "Node 1 Name" is the main node to connect with other node and it wil be "Node 1 Name" in the connection and "name": "Node 2 Name" is the node connected to "Node 1 Name" will be "node": "Node 2 Name" in the connection section
Remember `name` must be use exact the same in `connection` if not it will fail
 
