### 3. Data that can change
"Any value that can be added or modified through the n8n UI must be warp in a "" in the exported n8n JSON; otherwise, import may fail."
For example:
  ```json
  {
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://localhost:4000/apixemhocphi",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonQuery": "{MSV: {{ $json.MSV }}}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        -1664,
        1360
      ],
      "id": "6e688f5a-6870-4d5e-a3af-c8a636c4dd09",
      "name": "Tra cứu học phí1"
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Tra cứu học phí1": {
      "main": [
        []
      ]
    }
  },
  "pinData": {},
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": true,
    "instanceId": "60d86e7bdc5c6b3ca0992c6420e8f1e15c2cb830138b7ce921d5c22ec3b66295"
  }
}
```
In the above example, "url": "http://localhost:4000/apixemhocphi", the "http://localhost:4000/apixemhocphi" segment is wrapped in a "" because the user can add and modify it, similar to "specifyBody": "json", "jsonQuery": "{MSV: {{ $json.MSV }}}", "method": "POST",
However, note that in the ""name": "Tra cứu học phí1", the user can freely change the name of the node, but "id": "6e688f5a-6870-4d5e-a3af-c8a636c4dd09", and "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest", cannot be change because it is default the metadata of n8n.
Remember event object like this {MSV: {{ $json.MSV }}}, still need to wrap in the "" in exported n8n JSON, example "jsonQuery": "{MSV: {{ $json.MSV }}}", and it will not cause error because it is default in n8n, and it not stringtify it just warp with "" like this "{MSV: {{ $json.MSV }}}"
